  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Whist. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Whist is the classic English partnership trick-taking game and ancestor of Bridge. 4 players, 2 teams. 52 cards, 13 each. Last card dealt (to dealer) turned face-up = trump. Eldest hand leads. Follow suit. Each trick over 6 = 1 point. Honours (A-K-Q-J of trump): 3 held = 2pts, 4 held = 4pts. Game to 5 (British) or 7 (American). Rubber = best of 3.',
    objective: 'Play a bridge-derived trick-taking hand adapted for three active players.',
    gameplay: 'Three players are active in each hand, while larger tables rotate participation. Bidding and trick play adapt bridge ideas to the three-hand structure.',
    keyRules: [
      'Invented as a bridge adaptation for three-hand card play.',
      'May be played by more than three players with only three active at one time.',
      'Uses bridge-family trick-taking principles.',
    ],
